card.statement:
Suppose $a,b,c\in\mathbb{C}$ are such that $\{a-b,a-c,b-c\}\cap \mathbb{Z}=\varnothing$.
If $R=(a,a-1,b|a,b|c)$, then
\begin{center}
\Stone{$a$}\Stone{$a-1$}\Stone{$b$}

[0.2pt] $T(R)$:= \Stone{$a$}\Stone{$b$}

[0.2pt] \Stone{$c$}

\end{center}
$d_{31}(T(R))=2$, $d_{32}(T(R))=1$, $d_{21}(T(R))=0$ and $d_{22}(T(R))=0$.
